
  #98 -- multi-mood word order: sampler vs exact drive
  n=1000 k=50 p=0.05 beta=0.06, 60 sentences, 3 seeds

  numpy_sparse
      SVO+SOV   3/6
      SVO+VSO   3/6
      SOV+OVS   6/6
      VSO+OVS   6/6
      TOTAL 18/24   single-mood floor 4/4

  numpy_exact
      SVO+SOV   4/6
      SVO+VSO   4/6
      SOV+OVS   6/6
      VSO+OVS   6/6
      TOTAL 20/24   single-mood floor 4/4

  READING

    M1 exact beats sparse:                  True   18 -> 20 of 24
    M2 gain concentrated in SVO+SOV:        True   shared-opening +1, others +1 over 3 pairs
    M3 single-mood floor holds on exact:    True   4/4

    THE SAMPLER WAS A LARGE PART OF THE PROBLEM. Every
    word-order number in this repo predates an `engine`
    parameter on WordOrderLearner and is therefore a sampler
    measurement; the arc programme in #92/#93/#95 was built to
    fix a failure the exact substrate does not fully have.
